From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:46:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: tell the eDP PHY when the link carries video

An eDP PHY may need one setting while the link trains and another once
it carries video. On the Surface Laptop 8, the Glymur (v8) eDP PHY
trains the panel at 5.4 Gbps on four lanes with its TX LDOs at the
training value, and the picture shows noisy bands until they are
switched to the video value. The DP controller gives the PHY no point
at which to make that switch.

Once the controller reports the main link ready for video on an eDP
connector, call phy_notify_connect() on its PHY. PHYs without a connect
operation are unaffected, as phy_notify_connect() returns 0 for them,
and the PHY driver decides for which versions and rates it acts. An
error from the PHY is returned to the stream enable path.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index 83b890d5bbf..bffbd90ea69 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2652,6 +2652,14 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_stream(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl, struct msm_dp_panel *
 	drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
 		"mainlink %s\n", mainlink_ready ? "READY" : "NOT READY");
 
+	/*
+	 * Tell the eDP PHY that the link now carries video, for PHYs that
+	 * use a different setting during training than for video.
+	 */
+	if (mainlink_ready &&
+	    panel->connector->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP)
+		ret = phy_notify_connect(ctrl->phy, 0);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
